@startuml template_fill
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

title Template Fill Pipeline

actor User
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "API" as API
participant "Content\nGenerator" as CG
participant "Fill\nEngine" as FE2
participant "Bedrock" as BR
database "Search\nIndex" as SI
database "Template\nStore" as TS

User -> FE: Select template + write prompt
FE -> API: POST /templates/{id}/fill
API -> TS: Get template file bytes
API -> SI: Search for relevant chunks

== Generate Phase (section by section) ==

API -> CG: generate_content(prompt, context, doc_titles)
CG -> BR: Title page prompt (~500 tokens)
BR --> CG: JSON {title, author, institution...}
CG -> BR: Abstract prompt (~800 tokens)
BR --> CG: JSON {body}
CG -> BR: Glossary prompt (~600 tokens)
BR --> CG: JSON {terms[]}
CG -> BR: Chapter prompt (~1500 tokens)
BR --> CG: JSON {title, sections[]}
CG --> API: Complete content package

== Apply Phase (single pass) ==

API -> FE2: apply_full(docx_bytes, content)
note right of FE2
  1. Replace SDT placeholders
  2. Remove MACROBUTTON fields
  3. Fill bibliography table
  4. Fill index table
  5. Replace static text
  6. Scale fonts for overflow
  7. Preserve page breaks
end note
FE2 --> API: Filled DOCX bytes

API --> FE: DOCX file download
FE --> User: Download filled document

@enduml
